# <%= current_page.data.title %>

Implement the generated `BooksApi` boundary with a thin controller, application service,
MapStruct mapper, internal entity, and predictable error handling.

## Outcome

The public API can create, retrieve, and list books in memory. This deliberately temporary storage
keeps the first application slice focused; Tutorial 4 replaces it with PostgreSQL.

## Prerequisites

- Complete [Tutorial 2](java-tutorial-02-design-api.html)
- Generate the API and confirm the service module compiles

## Fast track

1. Add packages for `controller`, `service`, `mapper`, `entity`, and `exception`.
2. Implement `BooksApi` in a controller that delegates to a constructor-injected service.
3. Keep generated API models separate from an internal `BookEntity` and map with MapStruct.
4. Store books temporarily in a thread-safe map and assign IDs in the service.
5. Translate `BookNotFoundException` and validation failures to `ErrorResponse`.
6. Compile, start the service, and exercise all three operations.

## Create the implementation files

Create the package directories under
`laa-spring-boot-library-tutorial-service/src/main/java/uk/gov/justice/laa/library/tutorial`.
Add `entity/BookEntity.java`:

```java
package uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.entity;

import lombok.AllArgsConstructor;
import lombok.Builder;
import lombok.Data;
import lombok.NoArgsConstructor;

@Data
@Builder
@NoArgsConstructor
@AllArgsConstructor
public class BookEntity {
  private Long id;
  private String title;
  private Integer publicationYear;
  private String isbn;
}
```

Add `mapper/BookMapper.java`:

```java
package uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.mapper;

import java.util.List;
import org.mapstruct.Mapper;
import org.mapstruct.Mapping;
import uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.entity.BookEntity;
import uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.model.Book;
import uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.model.CreateBookRequest;

@Mapper(componentModel = "spring")
public interface BookMapper {
  @Mapping(target = "id", ignore = true)
  BookEntity toEntity(CreateBookRequest request);
  Book toApi(BookEntity entity);
  List<Book> toApi(List<BookEntity> entities);
}
```

Add `service/BookService.java`:

```java
package uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.service;

import java.util.Comparator;
import java.util.Map;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.entity.BookEntity;
import uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.exception.BookNotFoundException;
import uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.mapper.BookMapper;
import uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.model.Book;
import uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.model.BookList;
import uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.model.CreateBookRequest;

@Service
public class BookService {
  private final Map<Long, BookEntity> books = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
  private final AtomicLong nextId = new AtomicLong();
  private final BookMapper mapper;

  public BookService(BookMapper mapper) {
    this.mapper = mapper;
  }

  public Book create(CreateBookRequest request) {
    BookEntity entity = mapper.toEntity(request);
    entity.setId(nextId.incrementAndGet());
    books.put(entity.getId(), entity);
    return mapper.toApi(entity);
  }

  public Book get(Long id) {
    BookEntity entity = books.get(id);
    if (entity == null) throw new BookNotFoundException(id);
    return mapper.toApi(entity);
  }

  public BookList list(int limit) {
    var selected = books.values().stream()
        .sorted(Comparator.comparing(BookEntity::getId))
        .limit(limit)
        .toList();
    return new BookList(mapper.toApi(selected), limit);
  }
}
```

Add `controller/BookController.java`:

```java
package uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.controller;

import org.springframework.http.HttpStatus;
import org.springframework.http.ResponseEntity;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RestController;
import uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.api.BooksApi;
import uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.model.Book;
import uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.model.BookList;
import uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.model.CreateBookRequest;
import uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.service.BookService;

@RestController
public class BookController implements BooksApi {
  private final BookService service;

  public BookController(BookService service) {
    this.service = service;
  }

  public ResponseEntity<Book> createBook(CreateBookRequest request) {
    return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(service.create(request));
  }
  public ResponseEntity<Book> getBook(Long id) {
    return ResponseEntity.ok(service.get(id));
  }
  public ResponseEntity<BookList> listBooks(Integer limit) {
    return ResponseEntity.ok(service.list(limit));
  }
}
```

Add `exception/BookNotFoundException.java` and
`exception/GlobalExceptionHandler.java`:

```java
package uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.exception;

public class BookNotFoundException extends RuntimeException {
  public BookNotFoundException(Long id) {
    super("Book %d was not found".formatted(id));
  }
}
```

```java
package uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.exception;

import jakarta.validation.ConstraintViolationException;
import org.springframework.http.HttpStatus;
import org.springframework.http.ResponseEntity;
import org.springframework.web.bind.MethodArgumentNotValidException;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.ExceptionHandler;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RestControllerAdvice;
import uk.gov.justice.laa.library.tutorial.model.ErrorResponse;

@RestControllerAdvice
public class GlobalExceptionHandler {
  @ExceptionHandler(BookNotFoundException.class)
  ResponseEntity<ErrorResponse> notFound(BookNotFoundException exception) {
    return response(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND, "BOOK_NOT_FOUND", exception.getMessage());
  }

  @ExceptionHandler({MethodArgumentNotValidException.class, ConstraintViolationException.class})
  ResponseEntity<ErrorResponse> invalid(Exception exception) {
    return response(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST, "INVALID_REQUEST", "Request validation failed");
  }

  private ResponseEntity<ErrorResponse> response(HttpStatus status, String code, String message) {
    return ResponseEntity.status(status).body(new ErrorResponse(status.value(), code, message));
  }
}
```

Compile before adding tests. `./gradlew :laa-spring-boot-library-tutorial-service:compileJava`
should end with `BUILD SUCCESSFUL`. Fix package names and generated method signatures before moving
on; do not change generated files to silence a mismatch.

## Follow the request through the packages

The generated interface owns routes and signatures. The
`BookController`
implements it, chooses HTTP status codes, and delegates. The
`BookService`
assigns IDs and owns create, lookup, and bounding rules. Constructor injection makes its dependency
visible and lets tests supply the mapper directly.

`BookEntity` is an application representation rather than an OpenAPI type. Keeping it separate
prevents public contract changes from silently becoming storage changes. The
`BookMapper`
declares transformations; MapStruct generates type-safe mapping code during compilation. Ignore
the server-assigned ID when converting a create request.

`BookNotFoundException` describes a domain failure without mentioning HTTP. A
`@RestControllerAdvice` translates it into status `404`, code `BOOK_NOT_FOUND`, and a useful
message. It translates validation failures to the same stable error shape.

## Beginner primer: keep boundaries narrow

A controller is an adapter between HTTP and application behaviour. It should not allocate IDs,
query storage, or map fields. A service coordinates application rules without constructing HTTP
responses. A mapper moves data between representations. An entity represents internal state.
Small package responsibilities make failures easier to locate and later storage changes easier.

Generated Java remains read-only. Implement the generated interface in maintained source rather
than copying its annotations or editing it. Compilation then reports contract drift immediately.

